menu "TMC2209 - Stepper Motor Driver (UART)"

    config TMC2209_RSENSE
        float "Sense resistor value (ohms)"
        default 0.11
        help
            Value of the current sense resistors on the board, in ohms.
            Default 0.11 — to be verified against schematic/BOM.
            Used for mA ↔ CS register conversion.

    config TMC2209_SELF_TEST
        bool "Enable TMC2209 pure-logic self-test"
        default n
        help
            Run pure logic self-tests on boot (CRC8, mA→CS, microstep→MRES,
            bit layout verification, etc.).  No hardware dependency.
            Prints PASS/FAIL per case, final line "SELF-TEST DONE: n/total PASS".

    config TMC2209_BRINGUP
        bool "Enable TMC2209 hardware bring-up test"
        default n
        help
            Run hardware bring-up tests after self-test:
            1. Read IOIN → VERSION check
            2. GCONF write + read-back
            3. IHOLD_IRUN set_current
            4. CHOPCONF set_microstep + read-back
            5. DRV_STATUS sanity check
            6. (optional) Spin test
            Final line "BRINGUP: PASS n/6".

    config TMC2209_SPIN_TEST
        bool "Enable spin test (requires BRINGUP)"
        default n
        depends on TMC2209_BRINGUP
        help
            Include the spin test in bring-up: enable driver, send 2000
            STEP pulses at ~500 Hz (1µs pulse width), then disable.
            Motor should rotate ~10 full steps (1/8 revolution at 8 microsteps).
            WARNING: make sure motor can move freely before enabling.

endmenu
